    {
      "block_id": "h2-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Consent Gates",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Every model observation collection is gated by active telemetry consent. The `observation_allowed_by_consent()` helper checks:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-21",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Observation Kind",
        "Required Active Scope"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`provider`",
          "`provider_model_benchmarking`"
        ],
        [
          "`local_model`",
          "`local_model_benchmarking`"
        ],
        [
          "`commercial_export`",
          "`commercial_dataset_license`"
        ],
        [
          "`public_aggregate`",
          "`aggregate_public_reporting`"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Active Consent Semantics",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A consent scope is considered **active** only when: 1. The consent record status is `GRANTED` (not `REVOKED`, `DENIED`, or `NOT_REQUESTED`) 2. The scope is present in the record's `scopes` list",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If consent is revoked or denied, `active_consent_scopes()` returns an empty list, even if scopes remain in the record. This means: - A revoked record still shows which scopes were originally granted (audit) - But no observation collection is allowed against a revoked record - The `has_commercial_dataset_license()` helper checks raw scope presence - The `has_active_commercial_dataset_license()` helper checks scope + status",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-25",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Content-Light Guarantee",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "All observation records carry `content_light_guarantee: true`. The `validate_observation_content_light()` function verifies:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- No field keys named `raw_prompt`, `prompt`, `raw_model_output`, `model_output`, `source_code`, `diff`, `stdout`, `stderr`, `api_key`, `access_token`, `refresh_token`, or `private_path` - No raw secrets in string values (API key patterns, private keys) - The shared redaction module (`rig_relay.evidence.redaction`) classifies these same field keys as `FORBIDDEN`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-28",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Confidence Labels",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Early-alpha confidence levels for ranking snapshots:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-30",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Sample Count",
        "Confidence",
        "Label"
      ],
      "rows": [
